    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "For $f(x)=x^2$, find the gradient of the secant through $P(1.5,2.25)$ and $Q(1.4,1.96)$, where $h=-0.1$.\n\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=2.5cm,y=1.2cm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black}]\n\\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\definecolor{secantorange}{HTML}{EF8B2C}\n\\draw[black,->] (0,0) -- (2.1,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[black,->] (0,0) -- (0,4.3) node[above] {$y$};\n\\draw[curveblue,thick,domain=0:2,samples=60,variable=\\x] plot ({\\x},{(\\x)*(\\x)});\n\\path (1.9,3.61) node[left] {$y=x^2$};\n\\draw[secantorange,thick] (1.05,0.945) -- (1.8,3.12);\n\\fill[black] (1.5,2.25) circle (1.5pt);\n\\fill[black] (1.4,1.96) circle (1.5pt);\n\\path (1.5,2.25) node[above left] {$P(1.5,2.25)$};\n\\path (1.4,1.96) node[below right] {$Q(1.4,1.96)$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]",
        "solution_text": "Keep the same order for both changes: $Q-P$.\n\n$\\begin{align*}\\Delta y&=1.96-2.25\\\\&=-0.29\\\\\\Delta x&=1.4-1.5\\\\&=-0.1\\end{align*}$\n\n$\\begin{align*}m_{\\text{secant}}&=\\frac{f(1.5+h)-f(1.5)}{h}\\\\&=\\frac{-0.29}{-0.1}\\\\&=2.9\\end{align*}$\n\nThe secant gradient estimates the tangent gradient at $P$. A smaller $|h|$ improves this estimate for this curve."
      }
    ],
    "methods": [
      {
        "id": "secant-difference-quotient",
        "description": "Calculate the secant gradient as the signed vertical change divided by the signed horizontal change, using the same point order in both subtractions. Positive and negative steps and different function values use this same method.",
        "sourceRef": "booklets/mathsmap-sources/Stage 6 Advanced/Introduction to Differentiation 1_Estimating Change.md lines 609–627, Investigation: Differentiation by First Principles"
      }
